/div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367805\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367805\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3658568</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Ulgungga</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Fang Chao-ying</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"798\" data-page-number=\"798\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/196\" data-page-index=\"196\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/196\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;196\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>ULGUNGGA</b> \u70cf\u723e\u606d\u963f (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u77f3\u7434\u4e3b\u4eba), d. 1846, age about 70 (<i>sui</i>), prince and poet, was a descendant in the seventh generation of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Jirgalang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Jirgalang\">Jirgalang</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. The latter was the first Prince Ch\u00eang (\u912d\u89aa\u738b), but when his second son, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Jidu\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Jidu\">Jidu</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], inherited the princedom, the designation Ch\u00eang was altered to Chien \u7c21. In 1748 the princedom was taken from Jidu's branch of the family and given to <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/T%C3%AA-p%27ei\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/T\u00ea-p&#39;ei\">T\u00ea-p'ei</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], a great-grandson of Jirgalang's brother. As T\u00ea-p'ei had no heir the rank was given to Citungga \u5947\u901a\u963f (d. 1763), a grandnephew of Jidu. In 1778 when Citungga's grandson, Jihana \u7a4d\u54c8\u90a3 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u6e05\u4fee\u9053\u4eba,&#32;1758\u20131784), held the title, Emperor Kao-tsung, remembering the services of Jirgalang in founding the empire, decreed that the designation, Ch\u00eang, should be restored. Jihana had a bent for literature and possessed some skill as a painter. Ulgungga, eldest son of Jihana, became the third Prince Ch\u00eang in 1794 and the twelfth inheritor of Jirgalang's princedom. His long life as a prince was uneventful, but he performed well the duties belonging to his station. He accompanied Emperors J\u00ean-tsung and Hs\u00fcan-tsung on some of their tours but, except for journeys to Mukden and Jehol, never went beyond the metropolitan area of Chihli. He spent his life collecting&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"799\" data-page-number=\"799\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/197\" data-page-index=\"197\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/197\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;197\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>paintings and antiques, cultivating plants, and composing poems. A small collection of his verse, entitled \u77f3\u7434\u5ba4\u7a3f <i>Shih-ch'in-shih kao</i>, was printed about the year 1845. The poems were written, for the most part, during his later years.\n</p><p>Two of Ulgungga's sons, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Su-shun\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Su-shun\">Su-shun</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] and Tuan-hua (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Su-shun\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Su-shun\">Su-shun</a></span>), were politically active at the close of the Hsien-f\u00eang period and precipitated the <i>coup d'\u00e9tat</i> of Empress <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Hsiao-ch%27in\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Hsiao-ch&#39;in\">Hsiao-ch'in</a></span> and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/I-hsin\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/I-hsin\">I-hsin</a></span>&#32;[<i>qq.&#8239;v.</i>] in 1861.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/167/23b\u201342a; 1/221/11a; 2/2/34b; \u4eac\u5e2b\u574a\u5df7\u5fd7 <i>Ching-shih fang-hsiang chih</i> 5/5a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Fang Chao-ying</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hsiao-ch'in"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/I-hsin"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Jidu"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Jirgalang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Su-shun"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/T\u00ea-p'ei"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ubai"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wan"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Fang Chao-ying"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 2\n | onlysection = ulgungga\n | previous = Ubai\n | next     = Wan\n | from     = 196\n | to       = 197\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Fang Chao-ying\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Ulgungga}}"}}}